.TITLE "nslookup"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays information that you can use to diagnose Domain Name System (DNS) infrastructure. It allows for querying __name servers__ to find IP addresses or domain names.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**nslookup domain_name**
Looks up the IP address for the specified domain name using the default DNS server.
> __domain_name__ the target domain

**nslookup ip_address**
Performs a reverse DNS lookup to find the domain name associated with an IP address.
> __ip_address__ the target IP

**nslookup domain_name dns_server**
Queries a specific DNS server for information about a domain name.
> __dns_server__ the target name server

**nslookup -type=mx domain_name**
Looks up the Mail Exchanger (MX) records for a specific domain.
> __-type=mx__ record type flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __nslookup__ in interactive mode allows you to perform multiple queries and change servers easily. It is an invaluable tool for verifying that DNS records have propagated correctly.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:ping** **windows:ipconfig**

